  "checks": [
    "A real compiled Tick first attempts an obstructed release. The deepest reported overlap matches an independent immediate service query. The callback-requested save retains the result and the current hand binding.",
    "A named drop input releases the animated prop from the pose reached on that exact tick, with the requested box frame and world velocities.",
    "The next compiled callback reads the prior result and the native outcome expires after that tick. Fresh owners reopen both blocked and successful saves and reproduce the full settled archive.",
    "A duplicate attachment command and a later invalid release roll back with byte-identical pre-batch saves, including the previous result. The successful release that precedes the invalid command does not leave a body or queued save.",
    "The 0.0.258 runtime rejects the new named feature at the same service extent on both backends. Unchanged 0.0.257 recoverable-grip modules keep working."
